WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.112 --> 00:00:01.979
("Dine With Kreisler" by Joseph Alexander)

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:04.025
- The first thing that you do is smell it.

00:00:04.025 --> 00:00:05.859
Then you go to swirl it.

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:09.301
And then I find out what
does it do on your tongue.

00:00:09.301 --> 00:00:10.896
Then you can really
experience the whole body

00:00:10.896 --> 00:00:11.896
of the milk.

00:00:18.673 --> 00:00:21.045
My name is Bas de Groot,
and I am the milk sommelier.

00:00:21.045 --> 00:00:25.212
70% of your flavor experience
is created by smell.

00:00:27.016 --> 00:00:30.662
My name is John Bucher,
and I'm a dairy farmer.

00:00:30.662 --> 00:00:32.670
We're in the heart of the wine country,

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:35.988
which is not typically
known as dairy country.

00:00:35.988 --> 00:00:37.961
- The main thing that I
do is telling the story

00:00:37.961 --> 00:00:40.990
of the rich diversity of milk.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:42.632
We come to waltz it.

00:00:42.632 --> 00:00:44.919
- Is that what you call it, waltz it?

00:00:44.919 --> 00:00:47.089
- Yeah, waltzing.

00:00:47.089 --> 00:00:48.115
- We call it swirl.

00:00:48.115 --> 00:00:49.477
- Oh okay, swirl.

00:00:49.477 --> 00:00:52.945
Milk and wine are both
made from living products.

00:00:52.945 --> 00:00:55.724
And one is made by soil and the plant,

00:00:55.724 --> 00:00:58.791
and the other one is also made
by the soil and the plant,

00:00:58.791 --> 00:01:02.190
but there is the cow between (cow moos).

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.115
We all think milk is
white, but only by seeing

00:01:05.115 --> 00:01:08.223
these two milks, we see
that milk is not white.

00:01:08.223 --> 00:01:11.209
- I see a really big difference in a way.

00:01:11.209 --> 00:01:12.542
- Do you see it?

00:01:13.591 --> 00:01:16.943
I think that milk can be
terroir, so where the cow lives,

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.602
in which landscape, like Sonoma County,

00:01:19.602 --> 00:01:23.734
but also the farmer and
his vision and his dreams.

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:26.483
That's all part of the terroir.

00:01:26.483 --> 00:01:29.240
- I'm very proud of what my parents did

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:30.780
to start this farm.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.964
Next year, we'll be here for 60 years.

00:01:33.964 --> 00:01:37.208
We operate a 700-cow organic dairy farm.

00:01:37.208 --> 00:01:39.299
We produce 5,000 gallons of milk a day.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:43.395
With that, I also farm
55 acres of wine grapes.

00:01:43.395 --> 00:01:47.248
Those of us that farm have
a tremendous responsibility.

00:01:47.248 --> 00:01:50.665
And that’s what's so exciting and fun for me,

00:01:53.158 --> 00:01:54.679
to be part of that.

00:01:54.679 --> 00:01:56.923
- John, what we have here is your milk.

00:01:56.923 --> 00:01:59.388
This is the milk of Clover Sonoma Organic,

00:01:59.388 --> 00:02:03.305
and we have the full-fats
and the two-percents.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:09.167
This is like fresh, sweet,
and then also having

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:10.652
a long aftertaste.

00:02:10.652 --> 00:02:12.496
Normally, I prefer the full-fat milk

00:02:12.496 --> 00:02:14.951
because fat is the carrier of taste.

00:02:14.951 --> 00:02:18.103
So, I'm really surprised
that I like two-percents.

00:02:18.103 --> 00:02:20.449
It has flavor, that's great.

00:02:20.449 --> 00:02:24.454
The milk, or the product of Farmer
John, is his own identity,

00:02:24.454 --> 00:02:26.293
and it's also something
that you can experience

00:02:26.293 --> 00:02:27.529
in the product.

00:02:27.529 --> 00:02:30.010
Farming is really about balance.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:32.544
As a farmer, you are standing
in front of an orchestra

00:02:32.544 --> 00:02:35.328
and try to make a really cool symphony.

00:02:35.328 --> 00:02:38.316
(cows moo)

00:02:38.316 --> 00:02:40.894
This is my first time being in California,

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.610
and I've now tasted the milk.

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:44.576
You really can experience the quality.

00:02:44.576 --> 00:02:46.076
This is good milk.

